(p)
to quantify;
(i)
The 'Death Benefit' to the surviving member or members of the family of the deceased Advocate;
(ii)
The grant to the Indigent and Disabled Advocates;
(q)
to decide the person or persons to whom the 'Death Benefit' should be given;
(r)
to call for the information and details as may be necessary from the concerned Bar Association and the members of the
family of the deceased advocate;
(s)
to make necessary enquiries, if required, before taking decision under these Rules;
(t)
to provide financial or other assistance to any advocate affected on account of any natural or unforeseen circumstances;
(u)
to formulate and implement any further or other scheme or schemes, for the benefit of advocates.
